{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 44","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In solving a problem that reduces to a quadratic equation one student makes a mistake only in the constant term of the equation and \nobtains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the roots. Another student makes a mistake only in the coefficient of the first degree term and \nfind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a483ee25b066703890405f0127fef9c31572fb81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> for the roots. The correct equation was: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0f8719cc674cb489de976e161eb6bf8d5a364f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ x^2-10x+9=0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ x^2+10x+9=0 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ x^2-10x+16=0\\\\  \\textbf{(D)}\\ x^2-8x-9=0\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/007a93ae8547c0b9531c77b9d8af131b0a278fbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+bx+c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> represent the correct equation. Since the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the sum of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa30e2beb1820f6b39f6251023709c8165cefc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-b$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> and the product of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>The first student has the correct first-degree term, so the sum of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a677eaa69013089776cc8196d7389fa023b3e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+2=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/9/d896da1471cc81b6260baac3a2d402f12b1c6ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />. The second student has the correct constant term, so the product of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/0/e80aa7d54be53bc64fd4ea199508f5f0dd780bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-9)(-1) = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcf069d8a6c65338cedd8d4d727c3dbbc81842b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=9$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, the correct equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078eab69f47fc9c0fec09afcdeb5aa2f32aa69ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } x^2-10x+9=0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"180\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_44&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_43\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 43\">Problem 43</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_45\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 45\">Problem 45</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=